    "lawCode": "Amd §22, Gen Con L",
    "lawSection": "General Construction Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8440\n\nSPONSOR: KRUEGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general construction law, in relation to requiring\nthe use of gender-neutral terms in law\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to require that gender-neutral terms be used\nin any law, local law, rule, regulation, ordinance or resolution.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section 1 requires that gender-neutral terms be used in any law, local\nlaw, rule, regulation, ordinance or resolution, including but not limit-\ned  to  \"they,\"  \"them\"  and  \"theirs.\" If a law, local law, rule, regu-\nlation, ordinance or resolution is in reference to  a  specific  person,\nthe  language  referring  to such person shall be gendered in accordance\nwith the gender identity of such person.\n\n  Section 2 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nGender neutral language makes clear that  one  type  of  person  is  not\nfavored  or  disfavored to participate in a particular activity, profes-\nsion, or other situation in which gendered terminology has  historically\nbeen  used.  The laws of New York State are equally applicable to every-\none, and the language used in our laws, local laws,  rules,  regulations\nshould  be  gender  neutral.  This  bill will ensure that gender neutral\nlanguage is used going forward.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
